<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot pork at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equated to FOB Omaha Basis as of 3:00 PM and compared to Friday's 3:00 PM close, fresh loins were 2.00-4.00 higher; butts steady; sknd. hams 1.00-2.00 higher; sdls. bellies 2.00 higher; lean trimmings steady to 1.00 higher. Trading was very slow, with light to moderate demand and light offerings, USDA Market News said. Note: USDA also corrected its Friday July 11 data as follows: Loads of Pork Cuts S/B 36.63 and Commodity Hams 20-26 lbs. S/B 1.0 LD at 68.00.</p>
